  "step_3": "The decision reason focuses on the arithmetic mean of the outcomes (ignoring probabilities), which would favor Lottery A (1250 vs. 1200). However, the individual explicitly disregards the difference in amounts and instead bases their decision on the probability of winning, preferring Lottery B due to its higher chance (34% vs. 33%) of a non-zero outcome. The individual does not mention or use the sum or average of the outcomes in any way. The information considered (probabilities of winning) and the justification (maximizing chance of winning) are entirely different from the decision reason's basis (mean of outcomes, ignoring probabilities). Therefore, there is no evidence that the individual used the specified decision reason. In fact, the reasoning process described contradicts the logic of the reason.",
  "final_assessment_score": 0
